acobian determinant of the transformation $T:(u,v,w)\\to(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))$, given that\n\n$$\nu=- 8 x\\qquad v=y\\qquad w=z.\n$$" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549253 1072 #uuid "13892e3f-d765-51b3-b960-59a3b31629f7" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549253 1074 "For a transformation\n\n$$\nT:(u,v,w)\\to(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)),\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T$ is $\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}$.\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}$, the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}$.\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}=-8 & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}=0 & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z}=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x}=0 & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y}=1 & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z}=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x}=0 & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y}=0 & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{vmatrix}-8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=-8\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=-8\\left(1\\cdot 1-0\\right) \\\\ &=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}&=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1} \\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549254 1080 "\\frac{3}{u v w}" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549254 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549254 1083 #uuid "1a667fa8-98a7-5e3a-8f33-7e8c395fff89" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549251 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549257 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549266 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549272 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549283 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549255 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549255 1077 "selection" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549255 1078 #edb/ref 17592186549272 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549255 1079 #uuid "1ae9d39c-099c-5bd8-a0ca-bc8e7b7b3159" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549256 1080 "1" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549256 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549256 1083 #uuid "1b9d74b8-e21a-5070-b867-4bb5e1c969bb" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549257 1080 "\\frac{1}{16}" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549257 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549257 1083 #uuid "2117d2fe-e22b-580e-b937-660440cfb351" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549258 1068 #edb/ref 17592186549270 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549258 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549258 1071 "Consider the transformation $T:(u,v,w)\\to (x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)).$ The inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}(x,y,z)\\to (u(x,y,z),v(x,y,z),w(x,y,z))$ is given by\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2\\left(xy\\right) \\\\ yz \\\\ xz\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the Jacobian determinant of $T.$\n\n*Hint: You can assume that $x,y,z>0.$*" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549258 1072 #uuid "28f499ce-a5b7-5f3f-90af-72bf76f6b98e" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549258 1074 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)},$ the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nu(x,y,z)=2\\left(xy\\right),\\,v(x,y,z)=yz,\\,w(x,y,z)=xz.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =2\\left(y\\right) & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & =2\\left(x\\right) & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂z} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =z & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂z} & =y \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & =z & \\,\\frac{∂w}{∂y} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂w}{∂z} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nScaling the three derivative rows by $2, 1, 1$ multiplies the determinant by $2$.\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2\\left(y\\right) & 2\\left(x\\right) & 0 \\\\ 0 & z & y \\\\ z & 0 & x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\left(y\\begin{vmatrix}z & y \\\\ 0 & x\\end{vmatrix}-x\\begin{vmatrix}0 & y \\\\ z & x\\end{vmatrix}\\right)\\\\  & =2\\left(y(xz-0)-x(0-yz)\\right)\\\\  & =2\\left(xyz+xyz\\right)\\\\  & =4 x y z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting down $\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}$ in terms of $u,$ $v,$ and $w,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\left(2xyz\\right) & =2\\left(2\\sqrt{(xyz)^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =2\\left(2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =2\\left(2\\sqrt{xy(yz)(xz)}\\right) \\\\  & =2\\left(2\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{u}{2}\\right)vw}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & ={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4 \\sqrt{u v w}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549259 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549250 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549259 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549265 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549259 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549273 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549259 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549280 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549259 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549284 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549259 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549259 1077 "selection" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549259 1078 #edb/ref 17592186549265 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549259 1079 #uuid "2c746ba5-b294-58eb-b858-b452b710eccc" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549260 1080 "6" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549260 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549260 1083 #uuid "2d993ae9-8ed2-5193-82c6-1154b2659b11" 13194139535963 17592186045443 tr