artial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}=-2 & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}=0 & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z}=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x}=0 & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y}=1 & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z}=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x}=0 & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y}=0 & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=-2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=-2\\left(1\\cdot 1-0\\right) \\\\ &=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}&=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1} \\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549264 1080 "\\frac{1}{25}" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549264 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549264 1083 #uuid "492caa10-5fcf-5397-b994-6b200973c910" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549265 1080 "- \\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549265 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549265 1083 #uuid "5081b46a-4548-5033-9007-286761c7841f" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549266 1080 "1" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549266 1082 #edb/