 ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{vmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=6\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=6\\left(1\\cdot 1-0\\right) \\\\ &=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}&=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1} \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549275 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2 \\sqrt{u v w}}" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549275 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549275 1083 #uuid "98b94f67-6fda-5dd5-838b-c871de8b8565" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549276 1080 "- \\frac{1}{8}" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549276 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549276 1083 #uuid "a0ca081f-4cd9-5b7f-aa44-2df4fd0e0372" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549277 1068 #edb/ref 17592186549286 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549277 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549277 1071 "Consider the transformation $T:(u,v,w)\\to (x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)).$ The inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}(x,y,z)\\to (u(x,y,z),v(x,y,z),w(x,y,z))$ is given by\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}3\\left({e}^{x}\\right) \\\\ 3\\left({e}^{x+y}\\right) \\\\ 2\\left({e}^{x+y+z}\\right)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the Jacobian determinant of $T.$" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549277 1072 #uuid "a4d85b42-ead4-58c7-a443-af6077a7bc6a" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549277 1074 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)},$ the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nu(x,y,z)=3\\left({e}^{x}\\right),\\,v(x,y,z)=3\\left({e}^{x+y}\\right),\\,w(x,y,z)=2\\left({e}^{x+y+z}\\right).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =3\\left({e}^{x}\\right) & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂z} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =3\\left({e}^{x+y}\\right) & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =3\\left({e}^{x+y}\\right) & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂z} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & =2\\left({e}^{x+y+z}\\right) & \\,\\frac{∂w}{∂y} & =2\\left({e}^{x+y+z}\\right) & \\,\\frac{∂w}{∂z} & =2\\left({e}^{x+y+z}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nScaling the three derivative rows by $3, 3, 2$ multiplies the determinant by $18$.\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3\\left({e}^{x}\\right) & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3\\left({e}^{x+y}\\right) & 3\\left({e}^{x+y}\\right) & 0 \\\\ 2\\left({e}^{x+y+z}\\right) & 2\\left({e}^{x+y+z}\\right) & 2\\left({e}^{x+y+z}\\right)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =18\\left({e}^{x}\\begin{vmatrix}{e}^{x+y} & 0 \\\\ {e}^{x+y+z} & {e}^{x+y+z}\\end{vmatrix}\\right)\\\\  & =18\\left({e}^{x}({e}^{2x+2y+z}-0)\\right)\\\\  & =18 e^{x} e^{x + y} e^{x + y + z}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting down $\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}$ in terms of $u,$ $v,$ and $w,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18\\left({e}^{3x+2y+z}\\right) & =18\\left({e}^{x+(x+y)+(x+y+z)}\\right) \\\\  & =18\\left({e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{x+y}\\cdot {e}^{x+y+z}\\right) \\\\  & =18\\left(\\left(\\frac{u}{3}\\right)\\left(\\frac{v}{3}\\right)\\left(\\frac{w}{2}\\right)\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & ={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u v w}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549278 1080 "\\frac{1}{64}" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549278 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549278 1083 #uuid "a50b2500-22cc-56bc-96fb-e31907f23529" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549279 1080 "u v w" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549279 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549279 1083 #uuid "a786dab9-5919-5759-956b-993feb670569" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549280 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549280 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549280 1083 #uuid "b0e0a6e3-94eb-5f33-b1b0-6e5fad482c0b" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549281 1080 "\\frac{1}{3 u v w}" 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549281 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535963 17592186045443 true] [17592186549281 1083 #uuid "b638164a-9ad0-5829-ae5a-23171cfb7180" 13194139535963 1